+ Public Hearings scheduled for Carolina Bays (SC 31) Extension - Horry County SC.Gov Skip to main content Government Administrator Appointed and Elected Officials Boards and Commissions Code of Ordinances County Council Departments Business Bid Opportunities Business License Hospitality Fee Register of Deeds Tax Payer Services Zoning Compliance Residents 311 Service Request Council Meetings & Agendas Flooding & Disaster Prep Land Info Tax Payer Services Things to Do Sign in Login Register News & Announcements - Infrastructure & Regulation Search News Home Articles Public Hearings scheduled for Carolina Bays (SC 31) Extension SCDOT & NCDOT to hold meetings on SC31 Extension Project Public Hearings scheduled for Carolina Bays (SC 31) Extension Back Infrastructure & Regulation Posted On: 9/2/2025 3:32:17 PM Updated On: 9/3/2025 7:00:28 AM 1 SCDOT & NCDOT to hold meetings on SC31 Extension Project The S.C. Department of Transportation (SCDOT) and N.C. Department of Transportation (NCDOT) will hold two public meetings for the proposed Carolina Bays Parkway (SC 31) Extension project. The project, which is part of RIDE 3, would extend Carolina Bays Parkway (S.C. 31) from its current location at S.C. 9 in Horry County, across the North Carolina state line to U.S. 17 in Brunswick County, North Carolina, near Shallotte. The proposed improvement is a multi-lane full access freeway partially on a new location. The primary purpose of the project is to improve transportation in the area by enhancing mobility and connectivity for traffic moving in and through the project area. The community is invited to attend the following public meetings to learn more about this project: - Monday, September 29, 2025 from 5 - 8 p.m. Sea Trail Convention Center 75-A Clubhouse Road Sunset Beach, NC - Tuesday, September 30, 2025 from 5 - 8 p.m. North Strand Recreation Center 120 State Highway 57 South Longs, SC NCDOT and SCDOT representatives will be available to answer questions and receive comments regarding the proposed project. The opportunity to provide verbal comments and/or submit written comments and questions will be provided. Each meeting will begin with an Open-House public meeting from 5 – 6:30 p.m. for the public to review information on the project, the environmental document and map of the recommended alternative. This open format will be followed by a formal presentation at 7 p.m. To learn more about the project, visit the designated Carolina Bays Parkway Extension website here . More details on this RIDE project also available here on Horry County’s infrastructure improvement website. Latest Public Safety Horry County Fire Rescue wins SCAC award for pre-hospital blood program General Horry County HOME Consortium applications now open General Early Voting underway for 2026 Statewide General Election Infrastructure & Regulation SC - 22 Extension Public Scoping meetings scheduled for November General Horry County marks opening of Central Coast Complex with ribbon cutting Infrastructure & Regulation McCormick Road to see partial closure for stormwater improvements www.horrycountysc.gov | HC Government A product of Horry County Government ©2026 by Horry County Government — All Rights Reserved. General Info PGEgaHJlZj0nbWFpbHRvOmluZm9AaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3YnPmluZm9AaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3Y8L2E+ Departments Employment News Online Services Search Site Map Tax Payer Services Legal Accessibility Statement Privacy Terms 
