+ Parks - Horry County SC.Gov Skip to main content Government Administrator Appointed and Elected Officials Boards and Commissions Code of Ordinances County Council Departments Business Bid Opportunities Business License Hospitality Fee Register of Deeds Tax Payer Services Zoning Compliance Residents 311 Service Request Council Meetings & Agendas Flooding & Disaster Prep Land Info Tax Payer Services Things to Do Sign in Login Register Parks & Recreation Locations & Facilities Locations Beach Accesses Boat Landings Parks Facilities Recreation Centers Race Series Home Departments Parks & Recreation Parks Parks Horry County Parks and Recreation operates a variety of parks throughout the County. From its largest facilities, like Vereen Memorial Gardens, Socastee Recreation Park, and the Bike and Run Park, to its smallest facilities like Frink Park, Horry County Parks and Recreation has something to offer everyone. Parks are open from dawn til dusk, unless special events are occurring. The following map and table identify all County parks and recreation centers. The Resources page will provide you to links to other public recreation opportunities available in the County Parks Parks of Note Horry County Bike & Run Park Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens Socastee Recreational Park The Bike & Run Park is quickly becoming a park of regional significance, attracting both local users and vacationers. This facility is located along the Intracoastal Waterway near River Oaks Drive in Carolina Forest. It includes 7 miles of mountain biking and hiking trails on 70 acres of open space. The park was developed through the vision and labor of volunteers on a county-owned drege spoil basin that provides drastic changes in elevation that cannot be found in other parts of the county. In addition to providing a venue for a variety of races, its parking area serves as the first official East Coast Greenway trailhead in the State of South Carolina. Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens is located along the Intracoastal Waterway in Little River on more than 115 acres of forest and marshland. This facility includes approximately 3 miles of nature trails and boardwalks that meander through its botanical gardens and along its waterfront. A small segment of the original Kings Highway, a colonial route between Boston and Charleston, still remains at the front of the property, behind the CB Berry Community Center. Beach Wheelchairs available by reservation for Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens. Call 843-381-8000 Monday through Friday 8 am – 5 pm or send an email to PGEgaHJlZj0ibWFpbHRvOmJlYWNod2hlZWxjaGFpckBob3JyeWNvdW50eS5vcmciPmJlYWNod2hlZWxjaGFpckBob3JyeWNvdW50eS5vcmc8L2E+ to reserve at least two days in advance. Socastee Recreational Park is located on a 91.5 acre property off of Enterprise Road and serves residents living in the southern end of the county. The facility boasts numerous multi-purpose fields, picnic areas, a disc-golf course, trails, and a playground. County Parks Vereen Memorial Gardens and CB Community Center 843-249-4157 2250 Hwy 179, Little River 29566 Monday - Friday (8 am - 5 pm) Saturday & Sunday (Closed) Located along the Intracoastal Waterway in Little River on more than 115 acres of forest and marshland, this facility includes approximately 3 miles of nature trails and boardwalks that meander through its botanical gardens and along its waterfront. A small segment of the original Kings Highway, a colonial route between Boston and Charleston, still remains on the property, behind the CB Berry Community Center. The Center provides space for recreational programming and community events. Like Us On Facebook Carolina Forest Recreation Center (843) 915-5332 Location: 2250 Carolina Forest Blvd, Myrtle Beach 29579 Monday - Thursday (8 am - 8 pm) Friday (8 am - 6 pm) Saturday (8 am - 12 pm) Sunday (Closed) Like Us On Facebook James Frazier Community Center (843) 397-1018 Location: 1370 Bucksport Rd, Conway 29527 Monday - Friday (8 am - 8 pm) Saturday (10 am - 6 pm) Sunday (Closed) Like Us On Facebook North Strand Recreation Center (843) 915-5331 Location: 120 S Hwy 57, Little River 29566 Monday - Thursday (8 am - 8 pm) Friday (8 am - 6 pm) Saturday (8 am - 12 pm) Sunday (Closed) Like Us On Facebook Socastee Recreation Park Location: 7485 Butler Rd, Myrtle Beach 29588 Socastee Recreational Park is located on a 91.5 acre property and serves residents living in the southern end of the county, off of Enterprise Rd. The facility has numerous multi-purpose fields, picnic areas, a disc-golf course, trails, and a playground. This facility attracts a variety of users, from tournament participants to families. Like Us On Facebook South Strand Recreation Center (843) 915-5333 9650 Scipio Ln, Myrtle Beach 29588 Monday - Thursday (8 am - 8 pm) Friday (8 am - 6 pm) Saturday (8 am - 12 pm) Sunday (Closed) Like Us On Facebook Splinter City (843) 915-5333 3383 Splinter City St, Myrtle Beach 29577 Open Daily - Free To Play Located at the corner of Farrow Parkway and Kings Highway, this 25 acre site is home to the Splinter City Disc Golf Course. The course is free to play and has two sets of tees, making it the perfect challenge for both new and experienced players. This park is a partnership between the City of Myrtle Beach and Horry County, with Horry County Parks and Recreation managing maintenance and operations. The Horry County Bike & Run Park Open daily 5AM – 8PM Location: 150 Frontage Rd B-2, Myrtle Beach 29579 The Horry County Bike & Run Park is located along the Intracoastal Waterway near River Oaks Drive in Carolina Forest. It includes 7 miles of mountain biking and hiking trails on 70 acres of land. The park was developed through the vision and labor of volunteers and provides drastic changes in elevation that cannot be found in other parts of the county. In addition to providing a venue for a variety of races, its parking area serves as the first official East Coast Greenway trailhead in the State of South Carolina. Like Us On Facebook Aynor Athletic Complex 201 Jordanville Rd, Aynor 29511 Bayboro Park 6386 Joyner Swamp Rd, Galivants Ferry 29544 Bike and Run Park 150 Frontage Rd B-2, Myrtle Beach 29579 Burgess Park 10299 Hwy 707, Myrtle Beach 29588 Carolina Forest Recreation Center 2250 Carolina Forest Blvd, Myrtle Beach 29579 Dog Bluff Park 2700 Dog Bluff Rd, Galivants Ferry 29544 Frink Park 1243 Jacks Circle Rd, North Myrtle Beach 29582 Green Sea Floyds Ballfields 5050 Tulip Grove Rd, Nichols 29581 Hibben Memorial Park 9680 Shore Dr, Myrtle Beach 29572 Huger Park Under Construction International Drive Fields 900 International Dr, Myrtle Beach 29579 James Frazier Community Center 1370 Bucksport Rd, Conway 29527 Little River Neck Park 4693 Little River Neck Rd, North Myrtle Beach 29582 Loris Nature Park 300 Loris Lions Rd, Loris 29569 McNeil Park 2093 Steritt Swamp Rd, Conway 29526 Michael Morris Graham Park 1450 Vereen Rd, Aynor 29511 Mt. Vernon Tennis Courts SC 366 & Red Bluff Rd, Loris 29569 North Strand Park 120 S Hwy 57, Little River 29566 Pee Dee Park 7203 Marsh Dr, Conway 29527 Popular Park 8531 Hwy 90, Longs 29568 Sam Cox Park at Waccamaw 2889 Lee’s Landing Cir, Conway 29526 Sandridge Park 3428 Kates Bay Hwy, Conway 29527 Sanford D. Cox Sr. Community Park at Garden City 470 Elizabeth Dr, Garden City 29576 Simpson Creek Park 1420 Loop Circle, Longs 29568 Socastee Landing and Park 4299 Peachtree Rd, Myrtle Beach 29588 Socastee Recreation Park 7485 Butler Rd, Myrtle Beach 29588 South Strand Recreation Center 9650 Scipio Ln, Myrtle Beach 29588 Vereen Memorial Gardens & CB Berry Community Center 2250 Hwy 179, Little River 29566 White Oak Park 2737 New Home Cir, Conway 29526 www.horrycountysc.gov | HC Government A product of Horry County Government ©2026 by Horry County Government — All Rights Reserved. General Info PGEgaHJlZj0nbWFpbHRvOmluZm9AaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3YnPmluZm9AaG9ycnljb3VudHlzYy5nb3Y8L2E+ Departments Employment News Online Services Search Site Map Tax 